1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,750
Greetings. Hey.

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:02,970
(Sheldon:)I brought Amy here

3
00:00:02,970 --> 00:00:05,220
(Sheldon:)to show her some of
the work I'm doing.

4
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:07,600
(Amy:)It's very impressive,
for theoretical work.

5
00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:11,760
(Sheldon:)Do I detect a hint
of condescension?

6
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,960
(Amy:)I'm sorry, was I being too subtle?

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:17,400
(Amy:)I meant compared to the
real-world applications

8
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,430
(Amy:)of neurobiology,
theoretical physics is--

9
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:21,630
(Amy:)what's the word I'm looking for?--
hmm, cute.

10
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:23,570
(Leonard and Wolowitz oohing)

11
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:27,320
(Sheldon:)Are you suggesting the
work of a neurobiologist

12
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:30,690
(Sheldon:)like Babinski could ever
rise to the significance

13
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:34,050
(Sheldon:)of a physicist like
Clarke-Maxwell or Dirac?

14
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:35,750
(Amy:)I'm stating it outright.

15
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:37,750
(Amy:)Babinski eats Dirac for breakfast

16
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:40,650
(Amy:)and defecates Clarke-Maxwell.

17
00:00:42,490 --> 00:00:44,660
(Sheldon:)You take that back.

18
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:47,530
(Amy:)Absolutely not.

19
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:48,760
(Amy:)My colleagues and I are mapping

20
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,730
(Amy:)the neurological
substrates that subserve

21
00:00:50,730 --> 00:00:51,880
(Amy:)global information processing,

22
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:53,980
(Amy:)which is required for
all cognitive reasoning,

23
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:57,690
(Amy:)including scientific inquiry,
making my research ipso facto

24
00:00:57,690 --> 00:00:59,020
(Amy:)prior in the ordo cognoscendi.

25
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:01,720
(Amy:)That means it's better
than his research,

